# VER - Identify the running system

```text
VER
VER /V
```

## Identify versions

VER displays the OS identification. /V adds subsystem information. A
utility's own /VER identifies that utility, for example HELP /VER.

## Show the banner

```text
:VER /BANNER
```

The leading colon selects VER.COM, which prints the startup banner. An
experimental disk can carry a newer utility while the banner still
reports the core release.
